\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Four basis vectors over different fields}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The basis #{(1,\qi,\qj,h)} of \ref{fdip-00V1}
continues to have #{4} vectors after scalar extension.
Modulo #{3}, the matrix realization of \ref{fdip-00V7}
places them in a two-by-two matrix algebra. What does
passing to its columns do to the full cochain module
and to the operator on it?}
